P1 (Required): 0\n79: - P2 (Suggestions): 5\n80: - Resolved: 1\n81: \n82: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n83: \n84: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n85: \n86: - Reading the committed diff of each pass-one fix against its owning test, rather than the old report text, showed all three `render.ts` fixes intact in one pass (iteration 1). The deleted 35-entry `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` map could have silently dropped a doctor bridge; a key-set comparison against `COMMAND_ROWS` proved it did not.\n87: - Comparing duplicate command strings in `COMMAND_ROWS` before trusting the new class lookup avoided a false finding (iteration 1): the only two duplicates carry the same class.\n88: - Measuring the CLI with and without the new compiled-route request settled a latency suspicion with numbers (88-98 ms vs 134-160 ms warm) instead of inference (iteration 2).\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n93: \n94: - Treating the new stderr cap as a pure win missed its cost until the test itself showed the busy marker disappearing past the cap (iteration 2). Reading the test's own assertion is what surfaced finding 2.\n95: - Withdrawing `iter2-P2-hook-health-doc-scope` in iteration 4 after checking the Codex/Cursor/Devin shims kept the report honest: a doc claim about \"hook runs\" does not cover the OpenCode plugin's separate delivery path (iteration 4).\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 18. SYNTHESIS\n100: \n101: Synthesis completed at 2026-11-13T12:10:58Z with stop reason `converged`: verdict PASS, hasAdvisories true, 0 P0, 0 P1, 5 active P2, 1 resolved, release-readiness `converged`. The lineage report is `review-report.md` in this directory. The merge reads `deep-review-findings-registry.json` for the authoritative counts.\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n106: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n107: ### **`getStatus` reporting an inert flag is harmless.** It is harmless to the brief, but it is the observable half of finding 1 and is cited there, not a