{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669641222,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa57c70001zvv7WUXOndsIQI","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daa56597001ForNzpDQQ3aS6Q","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b40c93529b51f06c","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"compiledRouteTopOnly|compiled_route_top_only","path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor"},"output":"Found 23 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:\n  Line 38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:\n  Line 135: `advisor_recommend` accepts eight options: `topK` sets how many candidates to return (1 to 10), `includeAttribution` adds per-lane score breakdowns, `includeAbstainReasons` surfaces why lower-ranked candidates were not selected, `confidenceThreshold` overrides the minimum surfaced confidence, `uncertaintyThreshold` overrides the maximum surfaced uncertainty and `includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. Passing `false` skips the compiled-route enrichment so no compiled-route subprocess starts. The prompt hooks send `true`, because a recommendation's `command` comes from its compiled route. `compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. Passing `true` looks up the compiled route for the first recommendation only, which saves one subprocess for each further hub. The prompt hooks send it as `true`, so only the top pick can carry a `command`. `surfaceHint` forwards a code surface the caller already knows, such as `SKILLED` (1 to 64 characters), to the compiled-route front door, which ignores an unknown one. `advisor_validate` requires `confirmHeavyRun: true` because it executes the full validation bundle (corpus, holdout, parity, safety, latency).\n\n  Line 184: | `advisor_recommend` | Recommend skills for a prompt (`topK`, `includeAttribution`, `includeAbstainReasons`, `confidenceThreshold`, `uncertaintyThreshold`, `includeCompiledRoute`, `compiledRouteTopOnly`, `surfaceHint`) |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md:\n  Line 32: A resident daemon started from an older build rejects the newer request options `includeCompiledRoute` and `compiledRouteTopOnly` with JSON-RPC error -32602. The protocol handshake cannot tell the builds apart. When the error message names one of those options and the request carried it, the CLI retries the call exactly once without the named option. A daemon that rejects `includeCompiledRoute` is too old for `compiledRouteTopOnly` as well, so that retry drops both. The keys live in `COMPILED_ROUTE_OPTION_KEYS` in `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`. Every other error path is unchanged. The retry keeps the answer but costs one extra round trip per call until the old daemon stops. After an upgrade the operator should stop the old daemon once and let the next CLI call start a current one.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:\n  Line 26: Before any CLI spawn the hook runs the casual-prompt gate. `/help`, short acknowledgements and prompts below the length threshold return `skipped` without spawning the CLI. The CLI request sends `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also sends `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup and only the top pick can carry a command. The hook keeps the `command` field on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:\n  Line 37: The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n\n  Line 69: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` | Automated test | `includeCompiledRoute: false` skips enrichment on fresh and cached returns. `compiledRouteTopOnly: true` looks up the first recommendation alone. A command that ranks through its own row is not offered again by its hub. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:\n  Line 298:     compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tools/advisor-recommend.ts:\n  Line 24:       compiledRouteTopOnly: { type: 'boolean', description: 'Attach compiled-route metadata to the first recommendation only (default false). Saves one compiled-route subprocess per further hub.' },\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:\n  Line 632:         : enrichCompiledRoutes(parsedCachedOutput, input.prompt, workspaceRoot, input.options?.surfaceHint, input.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly === true),\n\n  Line 707:       : enrichCompiledRoutes(parsed, input.prompt, workspaceRoot, input.options?.surfaceHint, input.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly === true),\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:\n  Line 241:       compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:\n  Line 58:             compiledRouteTopOnly: { type: 'boolean', description: 'Attach compiled-route metadata to the first recommendation only (default false). Saves one compiled-route subprocess per further hub.' },\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md:\n  Line 21: | `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:\n  Line 1529: const COMPILED_ROUTE_OPTION_KEYS = ['includeCompiledRoute', 'compiledRouteTopOnly'] as const;\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:\n  Line 133: Each route lookup starts a separate process. That costs time inside the hook's budget. So `advisor_recommend` gains the option `compiledRouteTopOnly`, which is off by default. Set to `true`, it looks up the route for the first recommendation only. The hook sends it as `true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. So only the top pick can carry a command in the hook.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:\n  Line 121:       options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n\n  Line 180:       options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:\n  Line 127:       JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'Recommend a skill.', options: { includeCompiledRoute: false, compiledRouteTopOnly: true } }),\n\n  Line 178:     expect(Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(daemon.calls[1]?.options ?? {}, 'compiledRouteTopOnly')).toBe(false);\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/README.md:\n  Line 46: | `advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` | Verifies that `includeCompiledRoute: false` skips enrichment on fresh and cached returns, that `compiledRouteTopOnly: true` looks up the route for the first recommendation alone and that a command ranking through its own row is not offered again by its hub. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts:\n  Line 93:         options?: { includeCompiledRoute?: boolean; compiledRouteTopOnly?: boolean };\n\n  Line 97:       expect(payload.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly).toBe(true);\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":23,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 23 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:\n  Line 38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-on