cause each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:\n  Line 241:       compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md:\n  Line 21: | `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:\n  Line 135: `advisor_recommend` accepts eight options: `topK` sets how many candidates to return (1 to 10), `includeAttribution` adds per-lane score breakdowns, `includeAbstainReasons` surfaces why lower-ranked candidates were not selected, `confidenceThreshold` overrides the minimum surfaced confidence, `uncertaintyThreshold` overrides the maximum surfaced un