EST` set, as the capture does, and prints each named skill's positive lane contributions. It ran from the repository root on the same commit. The output is verbatim.\\n154: \\n155: ```text\\...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin/iterations/iteration-003.md:\n  Line 68: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | `advisor-recommend.md:33-39` describes `includeCompiledRoute`, `compiledRouteTopOnly` and the \"one command never takes two slots\" rule; `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238-244` passes the first two, and `render.ts:223-237` renders one command per label. |\n\n  Line 100: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md:21` — the claim that the request goes on stdin with `--json -` and carries `includeCompiledRoute` and `compiledRouteTopOnly` matches `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:228-245`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:\n  Line 101: - [x] T013 State when one replay speaks for every runtime (`CO`). In the module header, after the comment line that ends `of whatever the session reader happened to retain.` (the sentence wraps over three comment lines), add a comment paragraph that holds these three sentences word for word: `The handler gives the head row its command under every request shape and every caller asks for the route of the top pick alone, so for a run made from that state on, the Claude hook's head is the head every runtime's reader got.` `A run stored before that state carries the Claude hook's replay, which could differ from the head a non-Claude reader saw, at the head row or at the partner of an ambiguous head.` `A runtime whose renderer differs would need its own replay.` This sentence is true only after phase 021 has landed 