opencode plugin bridge\\\"\\n9:   - \\\"advisor hook smoke tests\\\"\\n10: importance_tier: important\\n11: contextType: implementation\\n12: version: 3.6.9.0\\n13: ---\\n14: \\n15: # Skill Advisor Hook Reference\\n16: \\n17: ---\\n18: \\n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\\n20: \\n21: The Skill Advisor concern surfaces prompt-safe routing context at the moment a user submits a prompt: it scores the prompt against the maintained skill graph and, when a match clears the confidence threshold, injects a brief recommending the matching skill(s). The brief is advisory: it never replaces explicit skill loading, never persists raw prompt text, and never blocks the prompt on an advisor failure.\\n22: \\n23: The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and sp...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/logs/WG7-T030.out:\n  Line 7: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794589466189,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d5de1a5d001f6h6hj8ePGwkob\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d5ddfbfa001hwK2g25x0puKiy\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_dacda0e42cae42f693342cfa\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\"},\"output\":\"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md, lines 1-88\\n1: ---\\n2: title: \\\"advisor_recommend Command\\\"\\n3: description: \\\"Native command that returns prompt-safe skill recommendations with lane attribution, lifecycle metadata, fail-open freshness semantics and an optional compiled-routing enrichment.\\\"\\n4: trigger_phrases:\\n5:   - \\\"advisor_recommend\\\"\\n6:   - \\\"mcp recommend tool\\\"\\n7:   - \\\"native recommend\\\"\\n8:   - \\\"skill recommendation tool\\\"\\n9:   - \\\"compiledRoute enrichment\\\"\\n10: version: 0.9.4.0\\n11: ---\\n12: \\n13: # advisor_recommend Command\\n14: \\n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\\n16: \\n17: Expose the native scoring pipeline as a command that any runtime can call through the CLI front door, with prompt-safe attribution and lifecycle-aware redirects.\\n18: \\n19: ---\\n20: \\n21: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\\n22: \\n23: `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` implements the command. Input is validated by `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` (Zod strict). The public response always includes the resolved `workspaceRoot` plus `effectiveThresholds`, where `effectiveThresholds` publishes the active `confidenceThreshold`, `uncertaintyThreshold` and `confidenceOnly` mode after request overrides are merged with defaults. Output also carries prompt-safe `recommendations[]`, optional `laneBreakdown[]` when `includeAttribution: true`, lifecycle redirect metadata (`redirectFrom...\n  Line 12: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794589482205,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d5de5938001k2rC118GHBBKeV\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d5de2ba400107cNZ9fxGolAXN\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_1d620b8b5c1c4c4a880b4acd\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"advisor-tool-schemas\\\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\\\.ts:[0-9]\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"},\"output\":\"31:Each recommendation carries an optional `compiledRoute` field (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308`, `z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional()`). `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`'s `enrichCompiledRoutes()` attaches it only when at least one recommended `skillId` is both in the fixed 7-hub `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS` set and currently permitted by the tri-state `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag (`compiledRoutingEnabledForHub()`, from `../lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`). Otherwise the schema re-parse is skipped entirely and the output returns unchanged. When enrichment runs, `compiledRouteForRecommendation()` shells out to `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <skillId> --prompt-stdin`, writes the prompt to its stdin and attaches the parsed result. The one exception is a result whose `servingAuthority` is `\\\"legacy\\\"`: the field then stays absent, because a legacy sentinel is never surfaced as if it were a compiled decision. A subprocess failure is handled the same way: silently no `compiledRoute` field, with an optional debug-gated stderr breadcrumb via `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG`, so a probe failure degrades to exactly what an ineligible or flag-off recommendation already looks like. In short, `compiledRoute` is attached only for an eligible, flag-permitted hub that is genuinely serving compiled. It is intentionally absent for every other combination: flag off, h...\n  Line 16: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794589498001,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d5de948f001V7SfOxw3i5s2Fm\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d5de68b7001XRo5XxCcKz7Cdz\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_5d8aa51b40d540e18c9804de\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"compiledRoute|includeCompiledRoute|compiledRouteTopOnly|export const AdvisorRecommend|export const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts | head -40\",\"workdir\"