{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669872184,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa902fa001haxDLoDraQ2PiP","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daa8d96c001exAiU9DeFUNb8x","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4084f55bd95b97a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"offer\\|Also:\\|parent-named\\|policy\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | head -60"},"output":"7:// and verdicts per runtime and arm: how often an offered command was started,\n431:// The line a model prints about an offered command is the only evidence in the\n432:// transcript that it took the command, offered it or turned it down, so the\n442:  /\\bCOMMAND:[ \\t`\\[]*(\\/[A-Za-z0-9][\\w.:-]*)[ \\t`\\]]*(?:→|->)[ \\t`\\[]*(started|offered|declined)\\b/i;\n482: * offer reached it even when the turn declined the command, which the run line's\n483: * own offer field cannot show. The last matching line decides the state, because\n490: * @returns {{offerSeen: boolean, commandState: string|null}} Whether at least one\n493:export function offerSeenIn(events, expectedCommand) {\n495:  if (wanted === null) return { offerSeen: false, commandState: null };\n499:    offerSeen: seen.length > 0,\n816:// The ask policy tells the reader to offer the command in one question and wait, so\n817:// asking is that policy's own step. A run offered the command on a `COMMAND:` line,\n820:  if (offerSeenIn(events, command).commandState === 'offered') return true;\n847: * @param {{command?: string|null, owner?: string|null, wrote?: boolean, mode?: string|null, policy?: string|null, checkoutDir?: string|null}} facts\n849: *   its command names, the policy its row carries and the folder its checkout names.\n852: *   hub, `asked` when an ask row offered its command and waited, `improvised` when\n856:export function workflowPath(events, { command, owner, wrote, mode, policy, checkoutDir }) {\n869:  // The ask policy tells the reader to offer the command in one question and wait, so\n870:  // asking is that policy's own step rather than a path the run improvised.\n871:  if (policy === ASK_POLICY && wrote !== true && firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) === null\n883:// The two row shapes whose policy forbids an unasked write: an `ask` row\n884:// carries the policy, and a must-not-start row carries only its type, because\n885:// the corpus leaves the policy of every no-start row empty.\n897:// the model's own edit of a command it was offered.\n970: * @param {{expected_command?: string|null, expected_policy?: string|null, row_type?: string|null, prompt?: string|null}} row\n985:  const policy = typeof entry.expected_policy === 'string' ? entry.expected_policy.trim().toLowerCase() : '';\n987:  const guarded = policy === ASK_POLICY || rowType === MUST_NOT_START;\n1206:// The start rate is counted over the rows whose policy made a start the outcome to\n1210:// A policy block is keyed by the row's own policy, so only the three outcomes a\n1211:// row can ask for carry a bucket. A row with no policy is judged elsewhere.\n1218:    expected_policy: typeof row.expected_policy === 'string' ? row.expected_policy : null,\n1302:    expected_policy: 'start',\n1318:  const policy = typeof label.expected_policy === 'string'\n1319:    ? label.expected_policy.trim().toLowerCase()\n1321:  return START_POLICIES.includes(policy);\n1324:// The policy a row is bucketed under is its own expectation, normalised once so\n1326:function policyOf(label) {\n1327:  const policy = typeof label.expected_policy === 'string'\n1328:    ? label.expected_policy.trim().toLowerCase()\n1330:  return POLICY_KEYS.includes(policy) ? policy : null;\n1457:// The offer a turn received lives on its run line, because the hook's head is not\n1459:// has no answer, so a missing key is counted apart from an offer that named another\n1461:// only the first leads, so a command on the partner side was shown and not offered,\n1464:function offerOf(line, label) {\n1465:  const hasOffer = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(line, 'offeredCommand');\n1468:    offered: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n1469:      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n1470:    partner: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n1471:      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n1472:    offerFieldAbsent: !hasOffer,\n1493: *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offeredAsPartner: boolean,\n1494: *      offerSeen: boolean,\n1496: *      wrote: boolean, policy: string|null, unsafe: boolean, commandLines: number,\n1529:  const offer = offerOf(line, label);\n1530:  const seen = offerSeenIn(events, label.expected_command);\n1539:    offered: offer.offered,\n1540:    offerFieldAbsent: offer.offerFieldAbsent,\n1541:    offeredAsPartner: offer.partner,\n1543:    // so it is a fact about the session even when the run line holds no offer.\n1544:    offerSeen: seen.offerSeen,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7:// and verdicts per runtime and arm: how often an offered command was started,\n431:// The line a model prints about an offered command is the only evidence in the\n432:// transcript that it took the command, offered it or turned it down, so the\n442:  /\\bCOMMAND:[ \\t`\\[]*(\\/[A-Za-z0-9][\\w.:-]*)[ \\t`\\]]*(?:→|->)[ \\t`\\[]*(started|offered|declined)\\b/i;\n482: * offer reached it even when the turn declined the command, which the run line's\n483: * own offer field cannot show. The last matching line decides the state, because\n490: * @returns {{offerSeen: boolean, commandState: string|null}} Whether at least one\n493:export function offerSeenIn(events, expectedCommand) {\n495:  if (wanted === null) return { offerSeen: false, commandState: null };\n499:    offerSeen: seen.length > 0,\n816:// The ask policy tells