{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669886540,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa934790024bIx33cbGYofZt","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daa90ab7001R1440zA6BwMBSc","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1306ea118002801","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"Also: /doctor\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests .opencode/plugins/tests | head -30"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:67:    expect(rendered).toBe(expectedBrief(`Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.82/0.20 pass.\\nAlso: /doctor:git setup (${commandRowFor('command-doctor-git-setup')?.policy})`));\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:76:    expect(renderAdvisorBrief(result, { childSession: false })).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:77:    expect(renderAdvisorBrief(result, { childSession: true })).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84:    expect(renderAdvisorBrief(updateResult, { childSession: true })).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:update (parent-named only)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:94:    expect(rendered).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:update (ask)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:115:    expect(rendered).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)');\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:67:    expect(rendered).toBe(expectedBrief(`Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.82/0.20 pass.\\nAlso: /doctor:git setup (${commandRowFor('command-doctor-git-setup')?.policy})`));\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:76:    expect(renderAdvisorBrief(result, { childSession: false })).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:77:    expect(renderAdvisorBrief(result, { childSession: true })).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84:    expect(renderAdvisorBrief(updateResult, { childSession: true })).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:update (parent-named only)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:94:    expect(rendered).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:update (ask)');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:115:    expect(rendered).toContain('\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)');\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"Also: /doctor\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests .opencode/plugins/tests | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669884537,"end":1794669886540}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669904030,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa938f100172EvawfkNhK95k","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daa90ab7001R1440zA6BwMBSc","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-88bb815d0c1d11f2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"Also: /doctor\" . --include='*.md' --include='*.ts' --include='*.js' --include='*.cjs' --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=dist | grep -v \"tests\\|iterations\\|scratch\\|review\" | head -20"},"output":"./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/acceptance-criteria.md:62:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given the doctor command page and the command bridges README, When each is searched for the companion line, Then each shows it with `(<policy>)` and says when it is left out | `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)'` prints 1 for each file (T013, T014) | Unmet | - |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/goal.md:63:- [ ] `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)'` prints 1 for `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md` and 1 for `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` under `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:58:- [ ] T003 [C] Record each stale statement (`$SP/stale-before.txt`). Run `rg -n -F '17 cases' $TR $FM`, `rg -n 'command-attach.ts' $LR`, `rg -c 'commandOnlyMentioned' $LR`, `rg -n -F 'only the top pick can carry' $FA`, `rg -c -e 'mention|refus|question about' $FA`, `rg -n -F 'Also: /doctor:' $FD $BR $SKA/README.md` and `rg -c -e 'uncertainty' $FM`, and write each command with its output. Verify: the first `rg` prints one line for each of the two files, the third and fifth print nothing, the fourth prints one line, and the `Also:` search prints one line for `FD`, one for `BR` and one for `$SKA/README.md`, the last of which holds `(<policy>)`. When a statement is no longer in its page, write that into the file and mark the task that corrects it `[B]`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:87:- [ ] T013 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word (`FD`). In the paragraph that starts `The renderer reads a generated lookup of runnable strings`, replace the companion line the page shows, the code span that starts ``Also: /doctor:<command>``, with ``Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)``, and add after that sentence: `The policy is run, start or ask, and the line is left out when the head already names that command.` The same rule stands in `$SKA/README.md` on the line `stale-before.txt` records. Use its wording where the two would differ. Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)' $FD` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'left out when the head already names that command' $FD` prints 1, `DOC $FD` exits 0 and `CAT` exits 0.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/plan.md:93:- Same-class producers: `rg -l -F '17 cases' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/changelog/**'` and `rg -l -F 'Also: /doctor:' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/changelog/**'`, so no third page keeps a stale copy.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:89:doctor-command-routing.md:35: ... When a skill is first and a doctor bridge also passes, the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> < ...\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:91:README.md:121: ... the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, and leaves the line out when the head alread ...\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:168:| REQ-007 | `doctor-command-routing.md` and `command-bridges/README.md` show the companion line as `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` and say it is left out when the head already names that command. |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/implementation-summary.md:55:The brief head is where a model learns which workflow fits the task. When Claude showed `use sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start)` and OpenCode showed `use sk-doc` alone, the same request reached a different choice on each runtime. This phase makes the head the same everywhere. The head row keeps its command whether the request asks for every row or the top only. The OpenCode plugin asks the advisor for the same top-only route the hooks ask for, and labels its head from the first row that passes, as the renderer does. The doctor companion line now prints its policy word, `Also: /doctor:update (ask)`, and is left out when the head or its partner already prints that command.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/implementation-summary.md:126:4. **Two pages still show the companion without its policy word.** `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md` and `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` write `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>`. They are listed for the changelog entry the packet close writes.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/acceptance-criteria.md:62:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given the skill README and the hook reference, When each is searched for the companion line's form, Then both show `(<policy>)` | Observed: `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)'` over the README p