 (start)' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints nothing and `rg -c -F 'ambiguous: sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.95/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.92/0.12 pass.' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 2. The last three checks read the two ambiguous prompts: after T014 the partner row is the same on both paths. Evidence: `repro-after.txt`: `same head: true` 17, `same head: false` nothing, the playbook head 2, `command-doctor-` nothing, bare `Also:` nothing, `Also: /doctor:update` nothing, `vs sk-doc 0.93/0.12 pass.` 2, `vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start)` nothing, the ambiguous playbook line 2.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:205:- [x] CHK-042 [P2] `rg -n \"Also:\" $SKA/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md $SKA/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md $SKA/ROUTER.md` is read once, and a sentence that shows the line's literal form without a policy word is listed in `implementation-summary.md` for the packet close. Evidence: the search was read once. `doctor-command-routing.md` and `command-bridges/README.md` show `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` without the word and are listed in Known Limitations item 4. `ROUTER.md` line 122 names the line without its literal form.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/spec.md:63:The recommend handler strips a command from the hub head whenever a lower row carries the same command, unless the caller asked for the top pick alone. The Claude hook asks that way and OpenCode does not, so `make a manual testing playbook for the login flow` reaches Claude as `use sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start)` and reaches an OpenCode model as `use sk-doc` with no command. The OpenCode plugin also labels the head from the first row the CLI returned, even when that row does not pass, so one prompt prints `use command-doctor-sk-skill-convert 0.95/0.12 pass.` with the scores of `sk-doc`. 