{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669965490,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daaa68ff002ouY0nMDNJZ9b6G","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daaa3ebf0011dEvKklCuoDYAt","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-beaacf7b71f7f57a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"command\\b\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts | head -30; echo ===; grep -n \"command\\b\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts | head -40"},"output":"64:  /** The skill whose workflow the command runs, so the two are never ranked as rivals. */\n67:  /** Set when the command's route only reads, so a list or show prompt may reach it. */\n83:    inventoryId: 'command-create-agent',\n87:    kind: 'command',\n89:    category: 'command',\n91:    description: 'Create command bridge for /create:agent OpenCode agent scaffolding.',\n93:    domains: ['create', 'agent', 'command'],\n101:    inventoryId: 'command-create-manual-testing-playbook',\n105:    kind: 'command',\n107:    category: 'command',\n109:    description: 'Create command bridge for /create:manual-testing-playbook manual testing playbook scaffolding.',\n111:    domains: ['create', 'testing', 'playbook', 'command'],\n119:    inventoryId: 'command-doctor-setup',\n122:    id: 'command-doctor-setup',\n123:    kind: 'command',\n125:    category: 'command',\n128:    keywords: ['set up skilled', 'help me set up skilled', 'is my skilled install healthy', 'skilled setup check', 'run the doctor setup checks', 'getting started with skilled', 'overview of every doctor command', 'model server or helper process still running after the session closed', 'list every check this project has', 'run every check in this project'],\n129:    domains: ['doctor', 'command'],\n138:    inventoryId: 'command-doctor-env',\n141:    id: 'command-doctor-env',\n142:    kind: 'command',\n144:    category: 'command',\n148:    domains: ['doctor', 'command'],\n157:    inventoryId: 'command-doctor-git-hooks',\n160:    id: 'command-doctor-git-hooks',\n161:    kind: 'command',\n163:    category: 'command',\n167:    domains: ['doctor', 'command'],\n176:    inventoryId: 'command-doctor-runtime-mirrors',\n179:    id: 'command-doctor-runtime-mirrors',\n===\n27:} from '../command-attach.js';\n108:const DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX = 'command-doctor-';\n561:// Explicit-lane evidence that a typed slash command named this skill.\n571:// command, the user has named it outright, so support it lends may lift a\n572:// target up to it but never past it; otherwise the command's own match is what\n573:// buries the command (a typed \"/deep:research\" handing its dependency enough\n597:  // Target skill -> the typed-command seed whose ceiling actually lowered it.\n633:  // A held seed can itself be held by another typed command, so each ceiling\n696:  // A command whose route only reads (a report, a status check) is the answer\n698:  // floor. A mutating command never carries the flag and stays gated.\n699:  if (skill.kind === 'command' && 'readOnly' in skill && skill.readOnly === true\n797:    if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-resume') return R.speckitResumeCommandPenalty;\n800:    if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-plan') return R.speckitPlanCommandBonus;\n819:  // Colon-command review-loop syntax (\":review:auto\") invokes the deep-review\n834:    if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-save') return R.saveContextMemorySaveBonus;\n842:    if (recommendation.skill === 'create:manual-testing-playbook' || recommendation.skill === 'command-create-manual-testing-playbook') return R.createTestingPlaybookBonus;\n857:// against a command row, with headroom, because a command offered for the wrong\n859:// over the next command and over the top skill, which is what kept a wrong\n860:// command out of first place on the tuning rows. Raise the bar before the\n867:// command on meaning, because the stand-in measures shared words rather than\n876:// A command bridge passes on its own wording: one of its authored phrases or its\n879:// its phrases are everyday words and a command must not be offered for a prompt\n885:// A question that only wants an answer must not be handed a command that\n888:// past that floor, so it has to ask the same question itself. A command whose\n890:// the answer. An explicit no-edit request rules out every command.\n898:  return skill !== undefined && skill.kind === 'command' && 'readOnly' in skill && skill.readOnly === true;\n910:    if (recommendation.kind !== 'command') continue;\n916:  // A command row with no cosine counts as 0, so the bar is the strongest other\n917:  // command row, not the strongest row overall: a skill row never decides this.\n926:    if (recommendation.kind !== 'command') return recommendation;\n994:// A typed command or matching doctor lead phrase moves its passing bridge first; otherwise passing\n1002:    recommendation.kind === 'command' && recommendation.skill.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX)\n1074:// A command that passed on meaning was chosen by the prompt's own words rather\n1076:// front of it. The command only takes the front when its cosine leads the top\n1079:// for the command to outrank.\n1091:    if (recommendation.kind !== 'command' || !meaningPassed.has(recommendation.skill)) continue;\n1099:    recommendation.kind !== 'command' && recommendation.passes_threshold\n1103:    // as 0 and the command's own cosine decides against it.\n1119:    if (row.command !== runnable || row.policy !== 'run') continue;\n1127:// decides whether the prompt is a doctor problem. If it is, the command it ranks\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"64:  /** The skill whose workflow the command runs, so the two are never ranked as rivals. */\n67:  /** Set when the command's route only reads, so a list or show prompt may reach it. */