{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670029113,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daab6571001gBz2KtBUN9dq8z","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daab05600012MjEvHR9ANGM1Q","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b3ca54f4def5d1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"childSession\\|AI_SESSION_CHILD\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib .opencode/plugins .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs | head -40"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:39:5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)`. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:49:   * to `AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`.\n.skilled/skill