{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670059280,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daabdbed001FrxPlBHRtZaRua","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daabb42f0010HN6XIcBdlusQP","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ade04551fa06799a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"companionLine\\|headPrintedCommand\\|companion\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:3:description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that give every runtime the same brief head: the head row keeps its command under every request shape, the companion line prints its policy word and never repeats a command, and the OpenCode head is labelled from the first passing row, each with a test written first.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:58:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `HEADS` after the build and write its output. Verify: `rg -c -F 'same head: false' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 4, `rg -c -F 'vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.93/0.12 pass.' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, which is the partner that carries a command on OpenCode alone, `rg -c -F 'opencode: Advisor: live; use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e 'Also: /[a-z:-]+( [a-z-]+)?\\s*$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints at least 2. When phase 020 has landed first, the raw-id line and some companion lines are already gone: record the counts found and keep the T011 expectations, which hold either way. Evidence: `repro-before.txt` on `7281629941`: `same head: false` 3 (planned 4), the partner `vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.93/0.12 pass.` 1, `opencode: Advisor: live; use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.` 2 (planned 1), companion `Also:` lines 0 (planned at least 2). Phase 020 landed first and removed the doctor offers these prompts drew, as this task foresees, so the counts are recorded and the T011 expectations stand.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:71:- [x] T004 [P] Print the policy word on the companion line (`RN`, `DBR`). Test first: in `DBR`, import `commandRowFor` from `../lib/command-attach.js` when absent. In the case `keeps the complete companion before directives under the default cap`, change the expected head to `` `Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.82/0.20 pass.\\nAlso: /doctor:git setup (${commandRowFor(<the bridge id that case passes>)?.policy})` ``, and in the case `uses the first doctor bridge after the top pick, past other skills`, change `'\\nAlso: /doctor:update'` to `'\\nAlso: /doctor:update (ask)'`. Add `it('prints the policy word of a companion and the child marker in a child session')`, which renders `advisorResult([{ skill: 'system-spec-kit', kind: 'skill', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12 }, { skill: 'command-doctor-env', kind: 'command', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.2 }])` twice, with `{ childSession: false }` and with `{ childSession: true }`, expecting `\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)` both times because a read-only run stays visible to a child, and renders the same head with `command-doctor-update` under `{ childSession: true }` expecting `\\nAlso: /doctor:update (parent-named only)`. Run `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and see the three expectations fail on the missing policy word. Then in `RN`'s `companionCommandLabel`, build the label as the command followed by ` (<word>)`, where the word is `policyWord(row?.policy, row?.mutating, childSession)`, and return the command alone when that word is `null`. Replace the comment above the function with one saying a companion is a command the reader may act on, so it carries the same policy word the head carries, and a child still gets the downgrade marker. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. When a golden brief in another file pins a companion with no policy word, update that one expectation and name the file in the task note. Evidence: worker log: first run `Tests  3 failed | 6 passed (9)` on the missing policy word, then `Tests  9 passed (9)`. Opus check PASS 2026-11-14: `VX` reruns `doctor-brief-render` 9 of 9, `render-child-session` 12 of 12, `command-head-length` 120 of 120, `command-brief-golden` 13 of 13, `TC` exit 0, no other golden file holds `Also: /`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:72:- [x] T005 Drop a companion that repeats a printed command (`RN`, `DBR`). After T004. Test first: in `DBR`, add `it('prints a command once when the head already names it')`, which renders a head row `{ skill: 'system-skilled-doctor', kind: 'skill', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.26, command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask', ownerSkillId: 'system-skilled-doctor' }` followed by `{ skill: 'command-doctor-update', kind: 'command', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.2 }`, widening `RecommendationInput` with the three optional fields, and expects the brief to contain `/doctor:update` exactly once and no `Also:`. Add `it('prints a second doctor bridge when the first repeats the head')`, with a third row `command-doctor-env`, expecting `\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)`. Run `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and see the first case print `Also: /doctor:update (ask)`. Then in `RN`'s `renderAdvisorBrief`, compute the head's printed command as `top.command ?? (top.needsMode === true ? undefined : commandRowFor(top.skill)?.command)`, and make the companion pick skip a row whose `doctorCommandString(row.skill)` equals it. In the ambiguous branch, also print no companion whose command equals the partner's `vs.command ?? commandRowFor(vs.skill)?.command`. Add a comment saying a command printed twice reads as two offers. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: worker log: first run `Tests  2 failed | 9 passed (11)`, one on `[ '/doctor:update', '/doctor:update' ]` printed twice, then 24 of 24 across the two files. Opus check PASS 2026-11-14: `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` 11 of 11, `tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` 13 of 13, `TC` exit 0, a render probe printed no repeated companion and kept a distinct one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:79:- [x] T007 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word in the skill README (`RM`). After T004. Replace ``the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` as its second line`` with ``the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)' $RM` prints 1. Evidence: coordinator check 2026-11-14: `G diff -U0 -- $RM` shows the one sentence replaced word for word and nothing else, and the verify `rg -c` printed 1. Noted, not changed: a child session prints `parent-named only` in place of the policy word, which the README sentence does not say.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:80:- [x] T008 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word in the hook reference (`HK`). After T004. In the paragraph that starts `The injected brief begins with`, find the sentence that says a doctor command appears on the top line or under a skill, and add after it: ``The line under a skill reads `Also: <command> (<policy>)`, and it is left out when the head or its partner already names that command.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: <command> (<policy>)' $HK` prints 1 and the added sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon. Evidence: coordinator check 2026-11-14: `G diff -U0 -- $HK` shows the one sentence added after the doctor-command sentence and nothing else, `rg -c -F 'Also: <command> (<policy>)'` printed 1, and the sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:158:- [x] CHK-013 [P1] The policy word comes from `policyWord`, the function the head uses, not from a second copy. Evidence: `companionCommandLabel` calls `policyWord(row?.policy, row?.mutating, childSession)` at `RN` line 264, the function the head uses at line 240.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:170:- [x] CHK-023 [P1] The child-flag run reports 0 failed, so the companion keeps its child marker (T009). Evidence: the child-flag run printed `Tests  16 passed (16)` (T009).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:179:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: A-2 and A-3 are `cross-consumer` (one handler, two request shapes), the OpenCode label is `instance-only`, A-7 and the second half of B-9 are `class-of-bug` in the companion line. Evidence: the plan addendum classes the findings as written here, and T003, T005, T006 and T014 fix them in place.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:182:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Matrix: request shape (top only, every row) by head kind (hub with a route, command row, doctor bridge) by companion (none, distinct, repeat), covered by T003 to T005 and the probe. Evidence: top-only and every-row by hub head are covered by `HRT` (7 passed), command-row and doctor-bridge heads with no, distinct and repeated companion by `DBR` (11 passed), and the probe prints 17 same heads.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:183:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Hostile state: the child-flag run in T009 proves the companion under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`. Evidence: the child-flag run under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` printed 16 of 16 (T009).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:203:- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `RM` and `HK` both show `(<policy>)` on the companion line (T007, T008). Evidence: T007 and T008 `rg -c` each printed 1.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:3:description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that give every runtime the same brief head: the head row keeps its command under every request shape, the companion line prints its policy word and never repeats a command, and the OpenCode head is labelled from the first passing row, each with a test written first.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:58:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `HEADS` after the build and write its output. Verify: `rg -c -F 'same head: false' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 4, `rg -c -F 'vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.93/0.12 pass.' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, which is the partner that carries a command on OpenCode alone, `rg -c -F 'opencode: Advisor: live; use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e 'Also: /[a-z:-]+( [a-z-]+)?\\s*$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints at least 2. When phase 020 has landed first, the raw-id line and some companion lines are already gone: record the counts found and keep the T011 expectations, which hold either way. Evidence: `repro-before.txt` on `7281629941`: `same head: false` 3 (planned 4), the partner `vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.93/0.12 pass.` 1, `opencode: Advisor: live; use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.` 2 (planned 1), companion `Also:` lines 0 (planned at least 2). Phase 020 landed first and removed the doctor offers these prompts drew, as this task foresees, so the counts are recorded and the T011 expectations stand.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:71:- [x] T004 [P] Print the policy word on the companion line (`RN`, `DBR`). Test first: in `DBR`, import `commandRowFor` from `../lib/command-attach.js` when absent. In the case `keeps the complete companion before directives under the default cap`, change the expected head to `` `Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.82/0.20 pass.\\nAlso: /doctor:git setup (${commandRowFor(<the bridge id that case passes>)?.policy})` ``, and in the case `uses the first doctor bridge after the top pick, past other skills`, change `'\\nAlso: /doctor:update'` to `'\\nAlso: /doctor:update (ask)'`. Add `it('prints the policy word of a companion and the child marker in a child session')`, which renders `advisorResult([{ skill: 'system-spec-kit', kind: 'skill', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12 }, { skill: 'command-doctor-env', kind: 'command', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.2 }])` twice, with `{ childSession: false }` and with `{ childSession: true }`, expecting `\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)` both times because a read-only run stays visible to a child, and renders the same head with `command-doctor-update` under `{ childSession: true }` expecting `\\nAlso: /doctor:update (parent-named only)`. Run `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and see the three expectations fail on the missing policy word. Then in `RN`'s `companionCommandLabel`, build the label as the command followed by ` (<word>)`, where the word is `policyWord(row?.policy, row?.mutating, childSession)`, and return the command alone when that word is `null`. Replace the comment above the function with one saying a companion is a command the reader may act on, so it carries the same policy word the head carries, and a child still gets the downgrade marker. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. When a golden brief in another file pins a companion with no policy word, update that one expectation and name the file in the task note. Evidence: worker log: first run `Tests  3 failed | 6 passed (9)` on the missing policy word, then `Tests  9 passed (9)`. Opus check PASS 2026-11-14: `VX` reruns `doctor-brief-render` 9 of 9, `render-child-session` 12 of 12, `command-head-length` 120 of 120, `command-brief-golden` 13 of 13, `TC` exit 0, no other golden file holds `Also: /`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:72:- [x] T005 Drop a companion that repeats a printed command (`RN`, `DBR`). After T004. Test first: in `DBR`, add `it('prints a command once when the head already names it')`, which renders a head row `{ skill: 'system-skilled-doctor', kind: 'skill', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.26, command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask', ownerSkillId: 'system-skilled-doctor' }` followed by `{ skill: 'command-doctor-update', kind: 'command', confidence: 0.82, uncertainty: 0.2 }`, widening `RecommendationInput` with the three optional fields, and expects the brief to contain `/doctor:update` exactly once and no `Also:`. Add `it('prints a second doctor bridge when the first repeats the head')`, with a third row `command-doctor-env`, expecting `\\nAlso: /doctor:env list (run)`. Run `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and see the first case print `Also: /doctor:update (ask)`. Then in `RN`'s `renderAdvisorBrief`, compute the head's printed command as `top.command ?? (top.needsMode === true ? undefined : commandRowFor(top.skill)?.command)`, and make the companion pick skip a row whose `doctorCommandString(row.skill)` equals it. In the ambiguous branch, also print no companion whose command equals the partner's `vs.command ?? commandRowFor(vs.skill)?.command`. Add a comment saying a command printed twice reads as two offers. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: worker log: first run `Tests  2 failed | 9 passed (11)`, one on `[ '/doctor:update', '/doctor:update' ]` printed twice, then 24 of 24 across the two files. Opus check PASS 2026-11-14: `VX tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` 11 of 11, `tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` 13 of 13, `TC` exit 0, a render probe printed no repeated companion and kept a distinct one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:79:- [x] T007 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word in the skill README (`RM`). After T004. Replace ``the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` as its second line`` with ``the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)' $RM` prints 1. Evidence: coordinator check 2026-11-14: `G diff -U0 -- $RM` shows the one sentence replaced word for word and nothing else, and the verify `rg -c` printed 1. Noted, not changed: a child session prints `parent-named only` in place of the policy word, which the README sentence does not say.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:80:- [x] T008 [P] Show the companion line with its policy word in the hook reference (`HK`). After T004. In the paragraph that starts `The injected brief begins with`, find the sentence that says a doctor command appears on the top line or under a skill, and add after it: ``The line under a skill reads `Also: <command> (<policy>)`, and it is left out when the head or its partner already names that command.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'Also: <command> (<policy>)' $HK` prints 1 and the added sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon. Evidence: coordinator check 2026-11-14: `G diff -U0 -- $HK` shows the one sentence added after the doctor-command sentence and nothing else, `rg -c -F 'Also: <command> (<policy>)'` printed 1, and the sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:158:- [x] CHK-013 [P1] The policy word comes from `policyWord`, the function the head uses, not from a second copy. Evidence: `companionCommandLabel` calls `policyWord(row?.policy, row?.mutating, childSession)` at `RN` line 264, the function the head uses at line 240.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:170:- [x] CHK-023 [P1] The child-flag run reports 0 failed, so the companion keeps its child marker (T009). Evidence: the child-flag run printed `Tests  16 passed (16)` (T009).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:179:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: A-2 and A-3 are `cross-consumer` (one handler, two request shapes), the OpenCode label is `instance-only`, A-7 and the second half of B-9 are `class-of-bug` in the companion line. Evidence: the plan addendum classes the findings as written here, and T003, T005, T006 and T014 fix them in place.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:182:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Matrix: request shape (top only, every row) by head kind (hub with a route, command row, doctor bridge) by companion (none, distinct, repeat), covered by T003 to T005 and the probe. Evidence: top-only and every-row by hub head are covered by `HRT` (7 passed), command-row and doctor-bridge heads with no, distinct and repeated companion by `DBR` (11 passed), and the probe prints 17 same heads.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:183:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Hostile state: the child-flag run in T009 proves the companion under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`. Evidence: the child-flag run under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` printed 16 of 16 (T009).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md:203:- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `RM` and `HK` both show `(<policy>)` on the companion line (T007, T008). Evidence: T007 and T008 `rg -c` each printed 1.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"companionLine\\\\|headPrintedCommand\\\\|companion\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/tasks.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670058477,"end":1794670059280}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794670062197,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"id":"prt_1daabea75001A0uKQU7Kxro8SV","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daabb42f0010HN6XIcBdlusQP","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"04891c211435d1a5e2b1d8408b76c45a153ac3a0","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1799,"output":176,"reasoning":542,"cache":{"read":220928,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794670065248,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"id":"prt_1daabf660001FpYqv4aBq9xjqh","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daabea7f001p3sDpSQivH4ngB","type":"step-start","snapshot":"04891c211435d1a5e2b1d8408b76c45a153ac3a0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670081350,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1daac3333001Mz7vadg54SN5H2","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1daabea7f001p3sDpSQivH4ngB","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3fdad566860891","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '225,255p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts; echo ===; sed -n '35,45p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md"},"output":"  readonly env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n  readonly timeoutMs: number;\n}): Promise<CliProcessResult> {\n  const payload = {\n    // The CLI refuses a longer prompt, so a longer one is sent as its head.\n    prompt: args.prompt.slice(0, ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n    options: {\n      topK: 3,\n      includeAttribution: false,\n      includeAbstainReasons: true,\n      // The hook reads nothing out of the compiled route itself. It asks for the\n      // route only because the advisor derives the slash command from it, and a\n      // recommendation with no command cannot tell the reader which mode to run.\n      includeCompiledRoute: true,\n      // Each route is a subprocess inside the hook's time budget, and the brief\n      // leads with the top pick, so only that one is looked up.\n      compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n      // Forward caller thresholds so the CLI scorer applies them; without this\n      // the scorer uses its own defaults and thresholdsFrom trusts the echoed\n      // defaults, silently discarding a caller's stricter thresholds.\n      confidenceThreshold: clampUnitThreshold(args.options.thresholdConfig?.confidenceThreshold, 0.8),\n      uncertaintyThreshold: clampUnitThreshold(args.options.thresholdConfig?.uncertaintyThreshold, 0.35),\n    },\n  };\n  return new Promise((resolvePromise) => {\n    let stdout = '';\n    let settled = false;\n    let timedOut = false;\n    const child = spawn(process.execPath, [\n      args.paths.cliPath,\n      'advisor_recommend',\n===\nThe request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n\nThe request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n\nA hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n\n### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n\nEach recommendation carries up to four optional fields that let a reader act on it without a second lookup. `kind` is `'skill'` or `'command'` and says which face the pick is, so a caller can tell a skill entry from a command row that scored as a candidate. `command` is the runnable slash string, such as `/speckit:save`. `policy` is `'run'`, `'start'` or `'ask'` and says how a caller may run that command. `ownerSkillId` names the skill that owns the command, which is the grouping key when several commands belong to one hub. All four stay optional in `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` so a response from a runtime that predates them still parses.\n\n`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads: `/doctor:env list` carries `read-only` and stays fully visible to a dispatched child, while `start`, `ask` and a writing `run` are marked as parent-named. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  readonly env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n  readonly timeoutMs: number;\n}): Promise<CliProcessResult> {\n  const payload = {\n    // The CLI refuses a longer prompt, so a longer one is sent as its head.\n    prompt: args.prompt.slice(0, ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n    options: {\n      topK: 3,\n      includeAttribution: false,\n      includeAbstainReasons: true,\n      // The hook reads nothing out of the compiled route itself. It asks for the\n      // route only because the advisor derives the slash command from it, and a\n      // recommendation with no command cannot tell the reader which mode to run.\n      includeCompiledRoute: true,\n      // Each route is a subprocess inside the hook's time budget, and the brief\n      // leads with the top pick, so only that one is looked up.\n      compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n      // Forward caller thresholds so the CLI scorer applies them; without this\n      // the scorer uses its own defaults and thresholdsFrom trusts the echoed\n      // defaults, silently discarding a caller's stricter thresholds.\n      confidenceThreshold: clampUnitThreshold(args.options.thresholdConfig?.confidenceThreshold, 0.8),\n      uncertaintyThreshold: clampUnitThreshold(args.options.thresholdConfig?.uncertaintyThreshold, 0.35),\n    },\n  };\n  return new Promise((resolvePromise) => {\n    let stdout = '';\n    let settled = false;\n    let timedOut = false;\n    const child = spawn(process.execPath, [\n      args.paths.cliPath,\n      'advisor_recommend',\n===\nThe request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n\nThe request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n\nA hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n\n### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n\nEach recommendation carries up to four optional fields that let a reader act on it without a second lookup. `kind` is `'skill'` or `'command'` and says which face the pick is, so a caller can tell a skill entry from a command row that scored as a candidate. `command` is the runnable slash string, such as `/speckit:save`. `policy` is `'run'`, `'start'` or `'ask'` and says how a caller may run that command. `ownerSkillId` names the skill that owns the command, which is the grouping key when several commands belong to one hub. All four stay optional in `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` so a response from a runtime that predates them still parses.\n\n`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads: `/doctor:env list` carries `read-only` and stays fully visible to a dispatched child, while `start`, `ask` and a writing `run` are marked as parent-named. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '225,255p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts; echo ===; sed -n '35,45p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670080819,"end":1794670081350}}}}
