{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670608453,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab438720016aimFIBas522NQ","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dab3f9bd0016iuTyhv1dl5tsk","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a990189e104b0d87","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"first passing\\|top-only\\|topOnly\\|head.*command\\|command.*head\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md | head -20"},"output":"53:    { \"id\": \"iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:5\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG4\" },\n76:    { \"id\": \"WG4\", \"order\": 4, \"lane\": \"advisory\", \"title\": \"Routing-accuracy README and transcript scorer\", \"files\": [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\"], \"findings\": [\"iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode\", \"iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report\"], \"alsoWrites\": \"The README lines for the WG2 and WG3 behaviour, using the names fixed in section 4\" },\n114:    \"score-command-transcripts session mode and header\",\n155:| iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report | accuracy-runner-2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:5-8` | introduced | Make the header describe the counts and verdicts the CLI prints |\n233:- **iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored** The capture sets `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC`, `VITEST`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL` and `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`. It deletes four more (`:361-376`). The `finally` block (`:662-668`) restores only the clock and removes the database folder. The header (`:31-33`) promises that a harness can import the module and score in-process without inheriting the projection. Test: in `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `process.env` after `scoreCommandCorpus()` equals a snapshot taken before. It fails today.\n276:4. **WG4 Routing-accuracy README and transcript scorer.** iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode and iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report. Files: `routing-accuracy/README.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. This group also writes the README lines for WG2 and WG3: `untrusted_checkout` in the backfill refusal list near `:75-77`, the `fixture` field, the g2 arm rule with `mixed_row_arms` and the cost script clearing `AI_SESSION_CHILD` near `:95-97`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"53:    { \"id\": \"iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:5\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG4\" },\n76:    { \"id\": \"WG4\", \"order\": 4, \"lane\": \"advisory\", \"title\": \"Routing-accuracy README and transcript scorer\", \"files\": [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\"], \"findings\": [\"iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode\", \"iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report\"], \"alsoWrites\": \"The README lines for the WG2 and WG3 behaviour, using the names fixed in section 4\" },\n114:    \"score-command-transcripts session mode and header\",\n155:| iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report | accuracy-runner-2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:5-8` | introduced | Make the header describe the counts and verdicts the CLI prints |\n233:- **iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored** The capture sets `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC`, `VITEST`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL` and `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`. It deletes four more (`:361-376`). The `finally` block (`:662-668`) restores only the clock and removes the database folder. The header (`:31-33`) promises that a harness can import the module and score in-process without inheriting the projection. Test: in `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `process.env` after `scoreCommandCorpus()` equals a snapshot taken before. It fails today.\n276:4. **WG4 Routing-accuracy README and transcript scorer.** iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode and iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report. Files: `routing-accuracy/README.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. This group also writes the README lines for WG2 and WG3: `untrusted_checkout` in the backfill refusal list near `:75-77`, the `fixture` field, the g2 arm rule with `mixed_row_arms` and the cost script clearing `AI_SESSION_CHILD` near `:95-97`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"first passing\\\\|top-only\\\\|topOnly\\\\|head.*command\\\\|command.*head\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670606450,"end":1794670608453}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794670612795,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"id":"prt_1dab4513b001Uh2COQC7MwMyBI","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dab3f9bd0016iuTyhv1dl5tsk","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"09ac4091da05b7409acffb84cca2b435531e4f7a","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":194,"output":91,"reasoning":957,"cache":{"read":274304,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794670616990,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"id":"prt_1dab4619e001etBQn66Gam4cjz","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dab45145001VIXsJstqpctPfJ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"026ef94ff870a7a7823c7e4de7f397924ca14dec"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670628625,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab489a9001nfYI6jyCJQRP7d","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dab45145001VIXsJstqpctPfJ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c6bfcd663e8db76","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"nl -ba .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md | sed -n '14,34p'; echo ===; nl -ba .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs | sed -n '150,192p'; echo ===; nl -ba .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js | sed -n '605,620p;848,865p'; echo ===; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts | sed -n '525,545p'"},"output":"    14\t---\n    15\t\n    16\t## 1. OVERVIEW\n    17\t\n    18\tThis package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n    19\t\n    20\tThe six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n    21\t\n    22\t---\n    23\t\n    24\t## 2. CONTRACT\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n    27\t- **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n    28\t- **Contained open.** A reader resolves its store path against the runtime's root before opening it, and opens the path its containment check resolved, so a path swapped after the check is not followed.\n    29\t- **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n    30\t- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n    31\t\n    32\t`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added. A Codex custom tool call has no JSON arguments, so its record carries the call's body as `arguments.input`, a string.\n    33\t\n    34\t- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n===\n   150\t  // Containment is decided before the file is opened, so a path outside the\n   151\t  // store is refused without its content ever being read.\n   152\t  const root = codexStoreRoot(options);\n   153\t  const containment = resolveInside({ path: transcriptPath, root });\n   154\t  if (!containment.ok) {\n   155\t    if (containment.code === 'session_mismatch') return containment;\n   156\t    try {\n   157\t      statSync(root);\n   158\t      return { ok: false, code: 'session_not_found' };\n   159\t    } catch {\n   160\t      return { ok: false, code: 'store_unreadable' };\n   161\t    }\n   162\t  }\n   163\t  const storePath = containment.path;\n   164\t\n   165\t  let raw;\n   166\t  try {\n   167\t    raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');\n   168\t  } catch {\n   169\t    try {\n   170\t      statSync(root);\n   171\t      return { ok: false, code: 'session_not_found' };\n   172\t    } catch {\n   173\t      return { ok: false, code: 'store_unreadable' };\n   174\t    }\n   175\t  }\n   176\t\n   177\t  const lines = parseJsonLines(raw);\n   178\t  if (recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath) !== sessionId) {\n   179\t    return { ok: false, code: 'session_mismatch' };\n   180\t  }\n   181\t\n   182\t  return {\n   183\t    ok: true,\n   184\t    source: {\n   185\t      runtime: RUNTIME,\n   186\t      sessionId,\n   187\t      locatorKind: LOCATOR_KIND,\n   188\t      storePath,\n   189\t    },\n   190\t    records: recordsFromLines(lines),\n   191\t  };\n   192\t}\n===\n   605\t  }\n   606\t\n   607\t  const data = parsed?.data && typeof parsed.data === 'object' ? parsed.data : null;\n   608\t  if (parsed?.status !== 'ok' || !data) {\n   609\t    return { brief: null, status: 'fail_open', error: 'UNEXPECTED_PAYLOAD', metadata: {} };\n   610\t  }\n   611\t\n   612\t  const recommendations = cliRecommendations(data, options);\n   613\t  // The renderer leads with the first passing row, so a label taken from a row\n   614\t  // that does not pass would name one row and score another.\n   615\t  const top = recommendations.find((recommendation) => recommendation.passes_threshold) ?? recommendations[0] ?? null;\n   616\t  // The CLI reports no freshness when it answered from the local scorer instead\n   617\t  // of the daemon; 'stale' keeps that brief renderable and honest.\n   618\t  const freshness = data.freshness === 'live' || data.freshness === 'stale'\n   619\t    ? data.freshness\n   620\t    : (parsed.degraded === true ? 'stale' : 'unavailable');\n   848\tfunction advisorCliRequest({ prompt, options, surfaceHint = null }) {\n   849\t  const requestOptions = {\n   850\t    // Three recommendations keep the two-target ambiguity line available without\n   851\t    // asking the advisor for a longer list than the brief can use.\n   852\t    topK: 3,\n   853\t    includeAttribution: false,\n   854\t    includeAbstainReasons: true,\n   855\t    // The brief prints the head and at most one partner, and every hook asks for\n   856\t    // the route of the top pick alone, so a partner that carried a command here\n   857\t    // and none there would give two runtimes two heads for one request.\n   858\t    compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n   859\t    confidenceThreshold: options.thresholdConfidence,\n   860\t    uncertaintyThreshold: DEFAULT_THRESHOLD_UNCERTAINTY,\n   861\t    ...(surfaceHint ? { surfaceHint } : {}),\n   862\t  };\n   863\t  const request = (text) => JSON.stringify({ prompt: text, options: requestOptions });\n   864\t  let remaining = options.maxPromptBytes - Buffer.byteLength(request(''), 'utf8');\n   865\t  let end = 0;\n===\n   525\t  }\n   526\t\n   527\t  const tokenCap = clampTokenCap(result.metrics?.tokenCap ?? options.tokenCap);\n   528\t  const thresholdConfig = options.thresholdConfig;\n   529\t  const childSession = options.childSession ?? process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1';\n   530\t  const recommendations = result.recommendations.filter((recommendation) => (\n   531\t    recommendation.passes_threshold === true\n   532\t    || (\n   533\t      recommendation.confidence >= (thresholdConfig?.confidenceThreshold ?? resolvedConfidenceThreshold())\n   534\t      && (\n   535\t        thresholdConfig?.confidenceOnly === true\n   536\t        || recommendation.uncertainty <= (thresholdConfig?.uncertaintyThreshold ?? resolvedUncertaintyThreshold())\n   537\t      )\n   538\t    )\n   539\t  ));\n   540\t  const [top, second] = recommendations;\n   541\t  if (!top) {\n   542\t    observeAdvisorPolicy(null, options);\n   543\t    return null;\n   544\t  }\n   545\t\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    14\t---\n    15\t\n    16\t## 1. OVERVIEW\n    17\t\n    18\tThis package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n    19\t\n    20\tThe six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n    21\t\n    22\t---\n    23\t\n    24\t## 2. CONTRACT\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n    27\t- **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n    28\t- **Contained open.** A reader resolves its store path against the runtime's root before opening it, and opens the path its containment check resolved, so a path swapped after the check is not followed.\n    29\t- **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n    30\t- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n    31\t\n    32\t`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added. A Codex custom tool call has no JSON arguments, so its record carries the call's body as `arguments.input`, a string.\n    33\t\n    34\t- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n===\n   150\t  // Containment is decided before the file is opened, so a path outside the\n   151\t  // store is refused without its content ever being read.\n   152\t  const root = codexStoreRoot(options);\n   153\t  const containment = resolveInside({ path: transcriptPath, root });\n   154\t  if (!containment.ok) {\n   155\t    if (containment.code === 'session_mismatch') return containment;\n   156\t    try {\n   157\t      statSync(root);\n   158\t      return { ok: false, code: 'session_not_found' };\n   159\t    } catch {\n   160\t      return { ok: false, code: 'store_unreadable' };\n   161\t    }\n   162\t  }\n   163\t  const storePath = containment.path;\n   164\t\n   165\t  let raw;\n   166\t  try {\n   167\t    raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');\n   168\t  } catch {\n   169\t    try {\n   170\t      statSync(root);\n   171\t      return { ok: false, code: 'session_not_found' };\n   172\t    } catch {\n   173\t      return { ok: false, code: 'store_unreadable' };\n   174\t    }\n   175\t  }\n   176\t\n   177\t  const lines = parseJsonLines(raw);\n   178\t  if (recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath) !== sessionId) {\n   179\t    return { ok: false, code: 'session_mismatch' };\n   180\t  }\n   181\t\n   182\t  return {\n   183\t    ok: true,\n   184\t    source: {\n   185\t      runtime: RUNTIME,\n   186\t      sessionId,\n   187\t      locatorKind: LOCATOR_KIND,\n   188\t      storePath,\n   189\t    },\n   190\t    records: recordsFromLines(lines),\n   191\t  };\n   192\t}\n===\n   605\t  }\n   606\t\n   607\t  const data = parsed?.data && typeof parsed.data === 'object' ? parsed.data : null;\n   608\t  if (parsed?.status !== 'ok' || !data) {\n   609\t    return { brief: null, status: 'fail_open', error: 'UNEXPECTED_PAYLOAD', metadata: {} };\n   610\t  }\n   611\t\n   612\t  const recommendations = cliRecommendations(data, options);\n   613\t  // The renderer leads with the first passing row, so a label taken from a row\n   614\t  // that does not pass would name one row and score another.\n   615\t  const top = recommendations.find((recommendation) => recommendation.passes_threshold) ?? recommendations[0] ?? null;\n   616\t  // The CLI reports no freshness when it answered from the local scorer instead\n   617\t  // of the daemon; 'stale' keeps that brief renderable and honest.\n   618\t  const freshness = data.freshness === 'live' || data.freshness === 'stale'\n   619\t    ? data.freshness\n   620\t    : (parsed.degraded === true ? 'stale' : 'unavailable');\n   848\tfunction advisorCliRequest({ prompt, options, surfaceHint = null }) {\n   849\t  const requestOptions = {\n   850\t    // Three recommendations keep the two-target ambiguity line available without\n   851\t    // asking the advisor for a longer list than the brief can use.\n   852\t    topK: 3,\n   853\t    includeAttribution: false,\n   854\t    includeAbstainReasons: true,\n   855\t    // The brief prints the head and at most one partner, and every hook asks for\n   856\t    // the route of the top pick alone, so a partner that carried a command here\n   857\t    // and none there would give two runtimes two heads for one request.\n   858\t    compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n   859\t    confidenceThreshold: options.thresholdConfidence,\n   860\t    uncertaintyThreshold: DEFAULT_THRESHOLD_UNCERTAINTY,\n   861\t    ...(surfaceHint ? { surfaceHint } : {}),\n   862\t  };\n   863\t  const request = (text) => JSON.stringify({ prompt: text, options: requestOptions });\n   864\t  let remaining = options.maxPromptBytes - Buffer.byteLength(request(''), 'utf8');\n   865\t  let end = 0;\n===\n   525\t  }\n   526\t\n   527\t  const tokenCap = clampTokenCap(result.metrics?.tokenCap ?? options.tokenCap);\n   528\t  const thresholdConfig = options.thresholdConfig;\n   529\t  const childSession = options.childSession ?? process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1';\n   530\t  const recommendations = result.recommendations.filter((recommendation) => (\n   531\t    recommendation.passes_threshold === true\n   532\t    || (\n   533\t      recommendation.confidence >= (thresholdConfig?.confidenceThreshold ?? resolvedConfidenceThreshold())\n   534\t      && (\n   535\t        thresholdConfig?.confidenceOnly === true\n   536\t        || recommendation.uncertainty <= (thresholdConfig?.uncertaintyThreshold ?? resolvedUncertaintyThreshold())\n   537\t      )\n   538\t    )\n   539\t  ));\n   540\t  const [top, second] = recommendations;\n   541\t  if (!top) {\n   542\t    observeAdvisorPolicy(null, options);\n   543\t    return null;\n   544\t  }\n   545\t\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"nl -ba .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md | sed -n '14,34p'; echo ===; nl -ba .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs | sed -n '150,192p'; echo ===; nl -ba .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js | sed -n '605,620p;848,865p'; echo ===; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts | sed -n '525,545p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670627241,"end":1794670628625}}}}
