{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670890499,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab8874e002jP1RKpnj59u7Mm","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dab8197f0017P4fRDL6rMKvo8","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5bddba52e034c81","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"top-only\\|top only\\|compiledRouteTopOnly\\|OpenCode plugin\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md | head -30"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/tasks.md:81:- [ ] T011 [P] Correct the top-only sentence and state when a command is withheld (`FA`). In the paragraph that starts `The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly``, replace `so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`` with `so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute`, and the first recommendation gets its `command` under every request shape`, after checking that sentence against the `## 021` block of `FACTS` and the handler line it names. Directly after the paragraph that starts `A hub also leaves `command` off`, add one paragraph of at most three sentences from the `## 020` block: `attachCommand()` returns no command when the prompt only mentions, refuses or asks about it, when the prompt rules out a change and when the prompt asks for a correction inside an existing readme, catalog or playbook. Verify: `rg -c -F 'only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`' $FA` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'under every request shape' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -e 'refuses or asks about' $FA` prints 1, `DOC $FA` exits 0 and `CAT` exits 0.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:61:A reader of the advisor's release notes learns nothing about the offer guards, the head parity, the workflow measure or the Codex fix, because the open entry covers phases 014 to 018 only. Six reference pages still describe the old behaviour, so a person who reads `advisor-recommend.md` is told only the top pick can carry a command under the top-only option, and two pages show the companion line without its policy word.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:86:# rg -n \"compiledRouteTopOnly\" feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md, line 37, cut.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:87:37:The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. ...\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:105:| `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` | Under the top-only option only the top pick can carry a command, and nothing says when a command is withheld | Phase 021 for the head row, phase 020 for the withhold |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:118:- Correct the `command-attach.ts` row, the two case counts, the top-only sentence, the meaning-pass bar and the two companion lines.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/spec.md:138:| `SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` | Modify | The top-only sentence and the withheld command |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","