{"type":"text","timestamp":1794671210195,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"id":"prt_1dabd0551002JOkyMLa5fJuqAX","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dabc5903001gAAefrNdwq5j06","type":"text","text":"Iteration 3 (maintainability) is a clean pass. Writing the narrative and final loop state, then checking convergence.","time":{"start":1794671183185,"end":1794671210195}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794671210237,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","part":{"partID":"prt_1dabd05800019RU4EMmcgPVzx5","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffe8tw0MjspShTXDB","messageID":"msg_1dabc5903001gAAefrNdwq5j06","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-905bb19e9e97ed81","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-4`, pass four)\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the seven rows of `review/review-scope-4.txt` for this area, plus the shared docs that state their contract.\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: the brief's \"docs that disagree with code\" and the changed-test surface. This iteration read the three changed test files against the branches they pin, the plugin renderer module's split and its new dead-line comment, and the adapter README's mapper claim. It also rechecked the two carried findings for a regression in the changed tests. No new defect was found.\n- Budget profile: `verify` (9 analysis actions)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.opencode/plugins/lib/skill-advisor-render.js:1-159` — fallback directive, setup regex, compiled-route summary and digest, the new comment at `:111-117`\n- `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs:360-470`, `:519-607`, `:650-675` — renderer helpers, first-passing-row, top-only request and timeout cases\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:1-187` — policy, child, repeat and sanitizer cases\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs:1-155` — custom body, function arguments, containment and failure cases\n- `.opencode/plugins/README.md:76`, `:157` — renderer module and mapper claims\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md:24-32` — reader contract and Codex body sentence\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:121` — carried finding R4-P2-003\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs:103-133`, `:142-192` — carried finding R4-P2-001\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:848-862` — carried finding R4-P2-002\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone. The two carried code/doc findings remain active; no new finding was found in the changed tests, the renderer module split or the adapter README claims.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The two active P2s are the only spec/code gaps: the Codex contained-open contract and the head command under a failing row 0. The tests pin every changed branch they claim to cover. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | Code pass; phase 021 tasks are the change record. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The renderer is shared; the plugin's top-only request matches the hooks; the child rule matches the spec-gate core; the Codex reader is the only reader with the unresolved-path read (finding R4-P2-001). |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | `advisor-recommend.md`'s top-only sentence remains the open phase 025 item; the changed tests and mapper claims agree with the code. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Dispatcher: `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md` owns the loop; this lineage writes only under `review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/`.\n- Append gateway: the iteration-2 receipt is `event-027859dd-1bcf-439d-a32c-cd637197e651`; the projection refreshed and the reducer reported 3 open P2, `corruptionCount: 0`.\n- Reducer: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` owns the registry, dashboard and strategy anchors.\n- Renderer module split: the plugin imports only `renderPluginFallbackDirective`, `SETUP_WORDING` and `FALLBACK_DIRECTIVE` from `lib/skill-advisor-render.js`; the compiled-route summary functions have no production caller (search returns only the test file), and the new comment at `:111-117` states that accurately.\n- Test surface: the plugin test's first-passing-row case (`:519-553`) exercises the plugin's own parsing; the renderer's `doctor-brief-render` cases exercise the public renderer; the Codex test exercises both the custom-call and function-call shapes through `loadSession`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **A future typed-command companion.** `companionCommandLabel` reads the generated row's policy, not a recommendation's own policy; no producer today attaches a doctor-bridge companion with a differing policy. Recorded in iteration 2; unchanged.\n- **A future enriched cache.** The prompt cache stores the un-enriched scorer output, so the route-option omission in the key is harmless today. If the cache ever stores enriched output, the key must include `includeCompiledRoute`, `compiledRouteTopOnly` and `surfaceHint`; recorded as a future risk, not a live finding.\n- **A custom call with both `arguments: \"{}\"` and `input`.** The body would be dropped by the `??` chain; Codex's current schema carries only `input`. Recorded in iteration 1; no finding.\n- **The plugin README's \"shared by the advisor plugin and its tests.\"** The module is shared as a module; the compiled-route half is test-only today, and the plugin README does not claim the plugin calls it. No finding.\n- **The `delays.includes(0)` timeout assertion.** It proves the SIGTERM timer is scheduled at the deadline minus the grace; `child.kills` still proves both signals were delivered. The case is robust to a busy machine, and no production branch is asserted away.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The plugin's timeout test now asserts the scheduled timer values and the delivered signal pair, so a machine-load flake no longer masks a wrong grace (`system-skill-advisor.test.cjs:650-675`).\n- The plugin's first-passing-row test asserts both the label and the two scores (`:533-534`), which is the exact wrong-result shape the old code produced.\n- The renderer's companion tests cover the policy word, the child marker, the repeated head command and the next-bridge fallback (`doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:61-116`).\n- The Codex tests cover the custom body, the parsed function arguments, the outside-store refusal and the header-id precedence (`codex.test.mjs:28-155`).\n- The mapper keeps `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` under the names `renderAdvisorBrief` reads; `kind` is not kept, but the plugin always passes the precomputed `ambiguous` boolean, so the renderer's `kind`-based re-derivation is not used (`render.ts:305-313`, `system-skill-advisor.js:626-632`).\n- No changed file contains a holdout or prompt-corpus reference; the search is clean for a third pass.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The plugin's top-only request is untested.** `tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs:575-585` asserts the request key; `handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` asserts the handler behaviour. The remaining gap is finding R4-P2-002, not a missing test.\n- **The compiled-route summary line is dead code that should be removed.** It is documented as intentionally kept for a future wiring at `lib/skill-advisor-render.js:111-117`; the plugin README says the module is shared, and the tests pin its behavior. No change request.\n- **The codex reader's custom body is untested through `readSession`.** The projection is generic over a valid `arguments` object, and the existing pairing test covers the tool-call/result path; the raw loader test is the right level for the body shape. No finding.\n- **The `parseCliResponse` first-passing selection duplicates the renderer's filter.** The two predicates use the same normalized threshold values (`normalizeThreshold` guarantees a number), and the plugin test pins the shared result. No finding.\n- **The new `delays.includes(0)` assertion can pass without a timer firing.** `child.kills` is asserted as `['SIGTERM', 'SIGKILL']`, so the timer firing is observed. No finding.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: synthesis\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry and the three iterations; no further code review.\n- Reason: convergence reached with all four dimensions covered and three active P2 advisories.\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: R4-P2-001, R4-P2-002 and R4-P2-003 are active.\n- Required evidence: the reducer-owned registry, the three iteration files and their deltas.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-4`, pass four)\\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the seven rows of `review/review-scope-4.txt` for this area, plus the shared docs that state their contract.\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: the brief's \\\"docs that disagree with code\\\" and the changed-test surface. This iteration read the three changed test files against the branches they pin, the plugin renderer module's split and its new dead-line comment, and the adapter README's mapper claim. It also rechecked the two carried findings for a regression in the changed tests. No new defect was found.\\n- Budget profile: `verify` (9 analysis actions)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.opencode/plugins/lib/skill-advisor-render.js:1-159` — fallback directive, setup regex, compiled-route summary and digest, the new comment at `:111-117`\\n- `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs:360-470`, `:519-607`, `:650-675` — renderer helpers, first-passing-row, top-only request and timeout cases\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:1-187` — policy, child, repeat and sanitizer cases\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs:1-155` — custom body, function arguments, containment and failure cases\\n- `.opencode/plugins/README.md:76`, `:157` — renderer module and mapper claims\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md:24-32` — reader contract and Codex body sentence\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:121` — carried finding R4-P2-003\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs:103-133`, `:142-192` — carried finding R4-P2-001\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:848-862` — carried finding R4-P2-002\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone. The two carried code/doc findings remain active; no new finding was found in the changed tests, the renderer module split or the adapter README claims.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The two active P2s are the only spec/code gaps: the Codex contained-open contract and the head command under a failing row 0. The tests pin every changed branch they claim to cover. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | Code pass; phase 021 tasks are the change record. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The renderer is shared; the plugin's top-only request matches the hooks; the child rule matches the spec-gate core; the Codex reader is the only reader with the unresolved-path read (finding R4-P2-001). |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | `advisor-recommend.md`'s top-only sentence remains the open phase 025 item; the changed tests and mapper claims agree with the code. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Dispatcher: `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md` owns the loop; this lineage writes only under `review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/`.\\n- Append gateway: the iteration-2 receipt is `event-027859dd-1bcf-439d-a32c-cd637197e651`; the projection refreshed and the reducer reported 3 open P2, `corruptionCount: 0`.\\n- Reducer: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` owns the registry, dashboard and strategy anchors.\\n- Renderer module split: the plugin imports only `renderPluginFallbackDirective`, `SETUP_WORDING` and `FALLBACK_DIRECTIVE` from `lib/skill-advisor-render.js`; the compiled-route summary functions have no production caller (search returns only the test file), and the new comment at `:111-117` states that accurately.\\n- Test surface: the plugin test's first-passing-row case (`:519-553`) exercises the plugin's own parsing; the renderer's `doctor-brief-render` cases exercise the public renderer; the Codex test exercises both the custom-call and function-call shapes through `loadSession`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **A future typed-command companion.** `companionCommandLabel` reads the generated row's policy, not a recommendation's own policy; no producer today attaches a doctor-bridge companion with a differing policy. Recorded in iteration 2; unchanged.\\n- **A future enriched cache.** The prompt cache stores the un-enriched scorer output, so the route-option omission in the key is harmless today. If the cache ever stores enriched output, the key must include `includeCompiledRoute`, `compiledRouteTopOnly` and `surfaceHint`; recorded as a future risk, not a live finding.\\n- **A custom call with both `arguments: \\\"{}\\\"` and `input`.** The body would be dropped by the `??` chain; Codex's current schema carries only `input`. Recorded in iteration 1; no finding.\\n- **The plugin README's \\\"shared by the advisor plugin and its tests.\\\"** The module is shared as a module; the compiled-route half is test-only today, and the plugin README does not claim the plugin calls it. No finding.\\n- **The `delays.includes(0)` timeout assertion.** It proves the SIGTERM timer is scheduled at the deadline minus the grace; `child.kills` still proves both signals were delivered. The case is robust to a busy machine, and no production branch is asserted away.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The plugin's timeout test now asserts the scheduled timer values and the delivered signal pair, so a machine-load flake no longer masks a wrong grace (`system-skill-advisor.test.cjs:650-675`).\\n- The plugin's first-passing-row test asserts both the label and the two scores (`:533-534`), which is the exact wrong-result shape the old code produced.\\n- The renderer's companion tests cover the policy word, the child marker, the repeated head command and the next-bridge fallback (`doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:61-116`).\\n- The Codex tests cover the custom body, the parsed function arguments, the outside-store refusal and the header-id precedence (`codex.test.mjs:28-155`).\\n- The mapper keeps `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` under the names `renderAdvisorBrief` reads; `kind` is not kept, but the plugin always passes the precomputed `ambiguous` boolean, so the renderer's `kind`-based re-derivation is not used (`render.ts:305-313`, `system-skill-advisor.js:626-632`).\\n- No changed file contains a holdout or prompt-corpus reference; the search is clean for a third pass.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The plugin's top-only request is untested.** `tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs:575-585` asserts the request key; `handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` asserts the handler behaviour. The remaining gap is finding R4-P2-002, not a missing test.\\n- **The compiled-route summary line is dead code that should be removed.** It is documented as intentionally kept for a future wiring at `lib/skill-advisor-render.js:111-117`; the plugin README says the module is shared, and the tests pin its behavior. No change request.\\n- **The codex reader's custom body is untested through `readSession`.** The projection is generic over a valid `arguments` object, and the existing pairing test covers the tool-call/result path; the raw loader test is the right level for the body shape. No finding.\\n- **The `parseCliResponse` first-passing selection duplicates the renderer's filter.** The two predicates use the same normalized threshold values (`normalizeThreshold` guarantees a number), and the plugin test pins the shared result. No finding.\\n- **The new `delays.includes(0)` assertion can pass without a timer firing.** `child.kills` is asserted as `['SIGTERM', 'SIGKILL']`, so the timer firing is observed. No finding.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: synthesis\\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry and the three iterations; no further code review.\\n- Reason: convergence reached with all four dimensions covered and three active P2 advisories.\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: R4-P2-001, R4-P2-002 and R4-P2-003 are active.\\n- Required evidence: the reducer-owned registry, the three iteration files and their deltas.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794671183232,"end":1794671210237}}}}
